<title>MEXICO: Mexico's capital account narrows in first quarter.</title>
<headline>Mexico's capital account narrows in first quarter.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's capital account posted a surplus of $1.869 billion in the first quarter of 1997, narrowing from $1.950 in the first quarter of 1996, Banco de Mexico said on Monday.</p>
<p>The following table details the capital account balance of payments. All figures are in billions of dollars:</p>
<p>					Q1 1997    Q1 1996</p>
<p>-----------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>    Overall balance		1.869	1.950</p>
<p>-----------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>    Liabilities		   -3.346	4.160</p>
<p>	Loans and Deposits	-7.026	0.972</p>
<p>	 Development Banks	-0.677	0.356</p>
<p>	 Commercial Banks	 -0.148	0.204</p>
<p>	 Banco de Mexico	  -2.525     -0.291</p>
<p>	 Public Sector	    -3.578	0.386</p>
<p>	 Private Sector	   -0.098	0.317</p>
<p>	Foreign Investment	 3.679	3.188</p>
<p>	 Direct			0.860	2.724</p>
<p>	 Portfolio		   2.819	0.465</p>
<p>	  Stock Market	     0.949	0.182</p>
<p>	  Domestic Denominated</p>
<p>	  Securities		 0.360     -1.445</p>
<p>	   Public Sector	   0.347	1.467</p>
<p>	   Private Sector	  0.013     -0.022</p>
<p>	  Foreign Denominated</p>
<p>	  Securities		 1.511     -1.162</p>
<p>	   Public Sector	   1.004     -1.229</p>
<p>	   Private Sector	  0.507	0.067</p>
<p>    Assets			   5.215     -2.211</p>
<p>	In Foreign Banks	   4.664     -2.263</p>
<p>	Exterior Credits	  -0.155     -0.150</p>
<p>Guarantees With</p>
<p>	Foreign debt		-0.172	0.301</p>
<p>	Others			 0.878     -0.098</p>
<p>    Errors And Omissions	 1.034	1.509</p>
<p>Variations in</p>
<p>    Net Reserves		   2.492	1.930</p>
<p>Adjustments in Gold-</p>
<p>    Silver and Valuation	 0.005	0.002</p>
<p>((--Robert Kozak, Mexico City newsroom +525 728 9559))</p>
